#DESCRIPTION
Inner-body (absorbing sphere) test: a uniform plasma streams in +x past an
absorbing sphere of radius 1.2 at the origin, declared with BODY.

Particles that enter a body cell are removed and tallied, no particle is
created inside the body, the electric field is pinned to zero inside the body
and the particle moments are reported as zero there, so the body must show up
as an empty hole with a wake downstream.

#INITFROMSWMF
F                       initFromSWMF

#GEOMETRY
-3.2                    xMin   [code units]
 3.2                    xMax
-3.2                    yMin
 3.2                    yMax
-0.05                   zMin   one cell: the invariant direction
 0.05                   zMax

#NCELL
64                      nCellX
64                      nCellY
1                       nCellZ

#MAXBLOCKSIZE
16                      maxBlockSizeX
16                      maxBlockSizeY
1                       maxBlockSizeZ

#PERIODICITY
T                       isPeriodicX
T                       isPeriodicY
T                       isPeriodicZ

BODY is only implemented for the full-PIC solver.
#SOLVEEM
T                       solveEM

#HYBRIDPIC
F                       useHybridPIC

#EFIELDSOLVER
1.0e-8                  tol
30                      nIter

#DISCRETIZATION
0.5                     theta
0.0                     coefDiff

#COMOVING
T                       solveFieldInCoMov
5                       nSmoothBackGroundU

Lax-Friedrichs upwind viscosity on the E equation (minmod limiter theta=1).
#UPWINDE
T                       useUpwindE
1                       limiterThetaE

Lax-Friedrichs upwind viscosity on the B equation + hyperbolic div-B cleaning.
#UPWINDB
T                       useUpwindB
1                       limiterThetaB

Digital-filter smoothing of the current density J.
#SMOOTHJ
T                       doSmoothJ
1                       nSmoothJ
0.5                     coefSmoothJ

#PLASMA
2                       nS
1.0                     mass           Species 0: ions
1.0                     charge
0.04                    mass           Species 1: electrons
-1.0                    charge

#UNIFORMSTATE
5.0                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 0: ions
100.0                   ux [km/s]      u_code = 1 (uNormSI = 1e5 m/s)
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
314000.0                T [K]
0.2                     rho [amu/cc]   Species 1: electrons (n_e = n_i)
100.0                   ux [km/s]
0.0                     uy [km/s]
0.0                     uz [km/s]
314000.0                T [K]
0.0                     bx [T]
0.0                     by [T]
3.0e-9                  bz [T]
0.0                     ex [V/m]
3.0e-4                  ey [V/m]       motional field E = -u x B
0.0                     ez [V/m]

The absorbing inner body: a sphere of radius 1.2 (code units, 12 cells) at
the origin. The unit here is the code length unit, not SI.
#BODY
sphere                  type
1.2                     radius [code units]
0.0                     center [code units] x
0.0                     center [code units] y
0.0                     center [code units] z

#TIMESTEPPING
T                       useFixedDt
0.02                    dt

#NORMALIZATION
1.0e5                   lNormSI   [m]
1.0e5                   uNormSI   [m/s]

#MONITOR
50                      dnReport

#SAVELOG
1                       dnSavePic
1                       dnSavePT

#PARTICLES
4                       npcelx
4                       npcely
1                       npcelz

#SAVEPLOT
1                       nPlot
z=0 var ascii pic       plotString
-1                      dn
0.5                     dt
1                       dx
body rhoS0 rhoS1 Ex Ey Ez Bx By Bz   plotVar

#STOP
-1                      MaxIter
2.0                     TimeMax

#RUN
